{"title":"Orthopaedic Appliance Specialist Roadmap","role":"Orthopaedic Appliance Specialist","summary":"An Orthopaedic Appliance Specialist works in the design, selection, fabrication, fitting, adjustment and maintenance of external devices that support or improve musculoskeletal function.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Prosthetics & Orthotics"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"An Orthopaedic Appliance Specialist works in the design, selection, fabrication, fitting, adjustment and maintenance of external devices that support or improve musculoskeletal function."},{"type":"h","text":"These may include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Orthoses"},{"text":"Braces"},{"text":"Splints"},{"text":"Supports"},{"text":"Spinal orthoses"},{"text":"Lower-limb orthoses"},{"text":"Upper-limb orthoses"},{"text":"Foot orthoses"},{"text":"Mobility-support devices"},{"text":"Rehabilitation-related appliances"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The professional works closely with orthopaedic surgeons, physiotherapists, occupational therapists, rehabilitation specialists and patients."},{"type":"p","text":"For specialized clinical prosthetics and orthotics practice, the exact professional qualification, registration and scope of practice depend on the applicable regulatory and institutional requirements. A general allied-health degree alone may not qualify someone for every specialized orthotist/prosthetist position."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Focus","Key Capabilities"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Human anatomy & biomechanics"},{"text":"Anatomy, physiology, movement"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Orthotic fundamentals"},{"text":"Materials, casting, device principles"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Clinical application"},{"text":"Assessment, fi